  "event_layout": "Opcode, row and column argument words, then 50 state words before scripted callee mutations. The original adapter captures EAX as row and EDX as column; the sole native boundary has exactly two int arguments.",
  "state_layout": "Arena and selected index; signed16 row/column fields; eight counts, eight probe and eight other raw waypoint DWORDs; eight FNV-1a32 fingerprints of complete queued paths. Probe index is fixed by the input, independent of count mutations. Other index is 1 when probe is 0, otherwise 0.",
  "final_layout": "Raw function result, the same state, and two full-arena FNV-1a32 fingerprints. Fingerprints are not literal full-byte trace comparisons.",
  "exact_no_write_check": "Original and native recorders snapshot both complete 150200-byte arenas, gameData and selection after initialization and after the sole callback mutation. Before the callback and at function return they directly compare all arena bytes and both globals with the latest snapshot. Empty cases use the initialization snapshot. Caller writes are rejected independently of the recorded fingerprints.",
  "before_comparison": "All 283 unchanged-before cases match the original and actual-after under GCC13 and Clang18 at O0/O2 (1132 comparisons on each native side), including all 48 backed raw-count cases. There is no uninitialized-local exclusion or repaired-before oracle. The old nested _DWORD count arithmetic wraps unsigned32; the tested stack/base arithmetic remains representable.",
  "path_scope": "Every conventional count 0..100 and 48 backed raw-count cases are represented. The address is path base plus raw count*4 modulo 2^32. Nonzero period aliases 0x40000000/0x80000000/0xC0000000 select the count word; their +1 aliases select waypoint 0. Other cases include period aliases of 2/99/100/101/102, ordinary 101/102 reading adjacent bytes and 0xFFFFFFFF reading four bytes before the path. The recorder validates each resolved four-byte address against actual arena backing; this does not assert that every uint32 count is readable.",
  "callee_return_scope": "The actual Map_GetBridgeCrossingCostOrZero implementation reads unsigned16 terrain and returns 5 for terrain 603..610, otherwise 0. There are 276 empty or 0/5 cases and seven separately named conditional callee-return cases. Negative, high-bit and other non-Boolean returns test this caller's nonzero-to-one normalization; they are not claimed as outputs of the actual callee.",
  "read_order": "Original gameData is loaded once at 0x454A3C; the count is checked at 0x454A44 and reloaded before the DWORD read at 0x454A7E. There are no intervening writes, callbacks or volatile declarations. Caching this stable base/count and decoding one four-byte local preserves the synchronous contract. Row and column are unsigned low bytes; the upper cost word is ignored. There are no caller state reads or writes after the callee result.",
  "compile_diagnostic_policy": "Actual-before and actual-after recorders use Wall/Wextra/Werror and UBSan with the established packed-layout alignment exception. No uninitialized or unused-variable diagnostic suppression is needed.",
  "negative_controls": [
    "wrong-empty-return",
    "capacity-clamp",
    "following-waypoint",
    "swapped-coordinates",
    "signed-row-byte",
    "bounded-selected-stack",
    "raw-callee-result",
    "positive-callee-result",
    "pre-callee-write",
    "post-callee-clear",
    "late-count-check",
    "unwrapped-address"
  ],
  "evidence": "artifacts/readability/road-functions-20260906/batch-15/original-proof/final-review/ and test-audit/final-review/ (private evidence). Initial original/candidate evidence remains preserved. Public tests require only tracked sources and this fixture; no retail bytes or assets are needed.",
  "limits": [
    "The unchanged 128 original instructions and actual native helper body execute. The neighboring 56-byte caller switch tables at 0x454AA0 are excluded from this function. Map_GetBridgeCrossingCostOrZero is a scripted recording/mutation boundary; actual terrain lookup does not execute in these traces.",
    "Two positive signed-low32 arenas provide four valid stack slots each. Invalid pointers, indices with overflowing source arithmetic, and raw waypoint addresses outside these arenas are excluded. No capacity clamp or policy for malformed paths is introduced.",
    "Unsigned byte forwarding through coordinates 255 is proven for backed path data. This does not establish actual map backing or gameplay reachability for every coordinate pair.",
    "Callback mutations test preservation and the absence of late state reads. They do not claim these mutations occur in the unmodified map query. Concurrent or volatile changes between ordinary reads are outside this synchronous proof.",
    "These function traces establish no runtime route, visual fidelity, mission arrival or campaign milestone."
  ]
}
